{
  "info": {
    "name": "Vio Backend API (v2 direct cut)",
    "_postman_id": "vio-backend-api-v2-2026-04-24",
    "description": "Source of truth for every HTTP request that hits (or is hit by) the Vio backend during the Apple TV → iOS cart-intent v2 flow.\n\n**Surfaces** (per `docs/API_V2_CONTRACT.md`):\n- `/v2/tv/*` — Apple TV + Android TV SDKs (apiKey)\n- `/v2/mobile/*` — iOS + Kotlin mobile SDKs (apiKey)\n- `/v2/commerce/*` — sponsor-scoped Commerce proxy (apiKey)\n- `/v2/admin/*` — platform admin (Bearer)\n- `/api/*` — dashboard operator (session cookie, unchanged)\n- Partner outbound — endpoints Vio CALLS on the partner (mock server today)\n\nEach request's **description** documents: purpose, caller, expected response, pre-conditions. Use this to verify every checkbox of the v2 smoke test before marking the flow green.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup & Health",
      "description": "Check that the backend + tunnel are up before running any flow.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /api/status — health check",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/status",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "status"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Returns 200 with `{status:\"ok\", timestamp}` if backend is reachable.\n\n**Called by**: Anyone (no auth).\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"timestamp\":\"<ISO>\"}`"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Apple TV SDK flow (/v2/tv/*)",
      "description": "Real sequence the Apple TV SDK executes during a session. Each request is what `VioTVManager` (on InteractiveAds-vio `main`) posts. Use the `apiKey` variable set to the TV2 client_app key (`tv2_api_key_91b4fbf634af4bc5` on dev).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1.1 POST /v2/tv/broadcast/subscribe (success path)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/tv/broadcast/subscribe",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "tv",
                "broadcast",
                "subscribe"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Combined TV bootstrap — validates broadcast ownership, ensures `end_users`, upserts `tv_sessions`, returns campaign + sponsors + wsUrl + capabilities.\n\n**Called by**: Apple TV SDK on `VioTV.connect(broadcastId:)` → `VioTVManager.subscribe` (Sources/VioTVCore/VioTVManager.swift).\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{subscribed:true, campaignId:36, broadcastId, sessionId, endUserId, wsUrl:\"wss://…/ws/36\", primarySponsor:{id, name:\"Elkjøp\", commerce:{apiKey,…}}, secondarySponsors:[], capabilities:{shoppable:true, engagement:<bool>}}`\n\n**Pre-conditions**: `broadcastId` exists, belongs to a campaign of the authenticated clientApp, campaign has `primarySponsorId`, clientApp has `tv_enabled=true` and platform in `tv_platforms`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"broadcastId\": \"{{broadcastId}}\",\n  \"externalUserId\": \"{{externalUserId}}\",\n  \"platform\": \"{{tvPlatform}}\",\n  \"tvDeviceId\": \"{{tvDeviceId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.2 POST /v2/tv/broadcast/subscribe (soft-miss: unknown broadcastId)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/tv/broadcast/subscribe",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "tv",
                "broadcast",
                "subscribe"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Validates the soft-miss path — backend returns 200 with `subscribed:false` so the SDK stays idle without raising errors.\n\n**Called by**: Same as 1.1 but with a broadcast the backend does not know.\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{subscribed:false, reason:\"broadcast_not_registered_for_client_app\"}` — `reason` also can be `campaign_has_no_primary_sponsor` or `tv_not_enabled_for_this_platform`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"broadcastId\": \"broadcast-no-existe-demo\",\n  \"externalUserId\": \"{{externalUserId}}\",\n  \"platform\": \"{{tvPlatform}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.3 POST /v2/tv/session/start (standalone, rare)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/tv/session/start",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "tv",
                "session",
                "start"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Registers a TV session without subscribing to a broadcast. Building block — most hosts use 1.1 which already upserts the session.\n\n**Called by**: Automation / custom hosts. Not called by the reference Apple TV demo.\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{sessionId:<int>, endUserId:<int>, startedAt:\"<ISO>\"}`",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"externalUserId\": \"{{externalUserId}}\",\n  \"platform\": \"{{tvPlatform}}\",\n  \"tvDeviceId\": \"{{tvDeviceId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.4 POST /v2/tv/session/heartbeat (every 60s while connected)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/tv/session/heartbeat",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "tv",
                "session",
                "heartbeat"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Keeps `tv_sessions.last_seen_at` fresh. Fired periodically by the SDK.\n\n**Called by**: `VioTVSessionManager.sendHeartbeat` (Sources/VioTVCore/Managers/VioTVSessionManager.swift:38) every 60s until `disconnect()`.\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{ok:true, lastSeenAt:\"<ISO>\"}`\n\n**Pre-conditions**: `sessionId` returned by 1.1 or 1.3.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"sessionId\": \"{{sessionId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.5 POST /v2/tv/broadcasts/:id/shoppable-ad (TV-side dispatch)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/tv/broadcasts/{{broadcastId}}/shoppable-ad",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "tv",
                "broadcasts",
                "{{broadcastId}}",
                "shoppable-ad"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Dispatches a shoppable ad via the TV SDK surface (`source=tv-sdk`). Persists `shoppable_ad_activations` row and broadcasts the `shoppable_ad` WS event to campaign subscribers.\n\n**Called by**: Rare from the real TV device — useful from automation or the smoke-test dispatcher. Operator path equivalent: `POST /api/broadcasts/:id/trigger-shoppable-ad` in folder 5.\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{success:true, activationId:<int>, product:{id,name,price}, sponsor:{id,name,avatarUrl,primaryColor}}` — and WS `shoppable_ad` fires to all clients on `/ws/36`.\n\n**Pre-conditions**: Campaign and broadcast exist; sponsor avatar present (422 `SPONSOR_MISSING_AVATAR` otherwise).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n  \"sponsorId\": \"{{sponsorId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.6 POST /v2/tv/cart-intent (remote tap on Apple TV)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/tv/cart-intent",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "tv",
                "cart-intent"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: TV-originated cart intent with v2 minimal body. Backend resolves `campaignId` + `sponsorId` from `shoppable_ad_activations[activationId]`, persists `cart_intents`, and forwards the envelope to the mobile user (WS direct → webhook/APNs fallback).\n\n**Called by**: `VioTVManager.sendCartIntent` (Sources/VioTVCore/VioTVManager.swift:87). Triggered by remote Select/Play.\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{success:true, cartIntentId:<int>, deliveryMode:\"websocket\"|\"dual\"|\"webhook\"|\"apns\"|\"dropped\"}` — and on the mobile side a `cart_intent` WS event fires if that user is connected.\n\n**Pre-conditions**: `activationId` must exist in `shoppable_ad_activations`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"externalUserId\": \"{{externalUserId}}\",\n  \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n  \"activationId\": \"{{activationId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.7 POST /v2/tv/session/end (disconnect)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/tv/session/end",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "tv",
                "session",
                "end"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Marks the TV session as ended. Fires on `VioTV.disconnect()`.\n\n**Called by**: `VioTVSessionManager.sendEnd` (Sources/VioTVCore/Managers/VioTVSessionManager.swift:42).\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{ok:true, endedAt:\"<ISO>\"}`",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"sessionId\": \"{{sessionId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. iOS Mobile SDK flow (/v2/mobile/*)",
      "description": "Real sequence the iOS SDK (`VioSwiftSDK` on `develop`) exercises during a campaign. Apple TV fires `shoppable_ad`; the iOS SDK is the receive side + performs its own cart-intent + device registration. All require `X-API-Key` with the mobile app client_app key.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "2.1 GET /v2/mobile/config (zero-config bootstrap)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/mobile/config",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "mobile",
                "config"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Returns active campaign + primarySponsor (with commerce block) + secondarySponsors + endpoints. Replaces `/v1/sdk/config` and `/v2/sdk/config`.\n\n**Called by**: `CampaignManager.bootstrapCommerceFromSdkConfig` (Sources/VioCore/Managers/CampaignManager.swift:712).\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{endpoints:{webSocketBase, commerceGraphQL}, campaign:{id:36,name,isPaused:false,…}, primarySponsor:{id:3,name:\"Elkjøp\",commerce:{apiKey,channelId,paymentMethods:[\"card\",\"klarna\",\"vipps\"]}}, secondarySponsors:[…], features:{engagement,shoppable,lineup}}`\n\n**Pre-conditions**: `apiKey` belongs to a clientApp that has an active campaign."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.2 GET /v2/mobile/broadcasts/:id/capabilities",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/mobile/broadcasts/{{broadcastId}}/capabilities",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "mobile",
                "broadcasts",
                "{{broadcastId}}",
                "capabilities"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Per-broadcast capability flags. Tells the SDK whether to boot engagement, shoppable, or lineup subsystems.\n\n**Called by**: iOS SDK before opening broadcast-scoped features.\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{broadcastId, campaignId, engagement:{enabled,hasPolls,hasContests}, shoppable:{enabled}, lineup:{available}}`"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.3 GET /v2/mobile/broadcasts/:id/components (placements)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/mobile/broadcasts/{{broadcastId}}/components",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "mobile",
                "broadcasts",
                "{{broadcastId}}",
                "components"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Active placements merged: campaign-wide + broadcast-scoped overrides. Each entry carries `sponsor.id` + a `commerce` block so the SDK can resolve per-sponsor Commerce credentials before rendering.\n\n**Called by**: 5 product views: VProductCarousel, VProductSpotlight, VProductStore, VProductBanner, VProductSlider.\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{broadcastId, components:[{id, campaignComponentId, type:\"product_carousel\", locationId, sponsor:{id,name,…}, commerce:{apiKey,channelId}, config:{productIds,…}}]}`"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.4 POST /v2/mobile/campaigns/:id/cart-intent (in-app cart-intent)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/mobile/campaigns/{{campaignId}}/cart-intent",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "mobile",
                "campaigns",
                "{{campaignId}}",
                "cart-intent"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Mobile-originated cart intent (user tapped \"Add to cart\" inside the iOS app itself). Optional `activationId` field closes the attribution chain if this intent came from a `shoppable_ad`.\n\n**Called by**: `VioCampaignPartnerAPI.sendCartIntent` (Sources/VioCore/Network/VioCampaignPartnerAPI.swift:26).\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{ok:true, cartIntentId:<int>, deliveryMode}` — persists `cart_intents` row.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"userId\": \"{{externalUserId}}\",\n  \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n  \"productName\": \"Samsung QLED\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.5 POST /v2/mobile/campaigns/:id/register-device (APNs/FCM)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/mobile/campaigns/{{campaignId}}/register-device",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "mobile",
                "campaigns",
                "{{campaignId}}",
                "register-device"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Registers APNs (iOS) / FCM (Android) device token so offline `cart_intent` events can reach the device via push. Backend also forwards the token to the partner's `partnerDeviceRegisterUrl` if set on the clientApp.\n\n**Called by**: `CampaignManager.submitApnsDeviceTokenForVioRegister` → `VioCampaignPartnerAPI.registerDevice` (Sources/VioCore/Network/VioCampaignPartnerAPI.swift:69).\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{success:true}` — also fires outbound `POST {partnerDeviceRegisterUrl}` (see folder 6).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"userId\": \"{{externalUserId}}\",\n  \"deviceToken\": \"apns-hex-<fill>\",\n  \"platform\": \"ios\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Commerce proxy (/v2/commerce/*)",
      "description": "Sponsor-scoped product catalog. Used by dashboard operator to pick products and by both SDKs to load product detail.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "3.1 GET /v2/commerce/sponsors/:id/catalog — sponsor-scoped catalog",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/commerce/sponsors/{{catalogSponsorId}}/catalog?limit=50",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "commerce",
                "sponsors",
                "{{catalogSponsorId}}",
                "catalog"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "50"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Fetches the Commerce GraphQL catalog filtered by that sponsor's `commerce_api_key` and `commerce_channel_id`.\n\n**Called by**: Dashboard `SponsorCatalogPicker`; iOS `ProductService.loadProduct(sponsorId:)` via `CommerceSdkClientProvider.client(forSponsorId:)`.\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{sponsorId, products:[{id,name,price,currency,imageUrl,…}]}` — empty array if the sponsor has no commerce key.\n\n**Pre-conditions**: Sponsor must have `commerce_api_key` set."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3.2 GET /v2/commerce/products — raw passthrough (debug)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/commerce/products?sponsorId={{catalogSponsorId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "commerce",
                "products"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "sponsorId",
                  "value": "{{catalogSponsorId}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Raw Commerce GraphQL proxy. Prefer 3.1 in runtime flows.\n\n**Called by**: Debug / power users.\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{products:[…]}`"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Admin API (Bearer)",
      "description": "Platform-admin dispatch. Requires `Authorization: Bearer <JWT>` (set `adminBearer` variable).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "4.1 POST /v2/admin/broadcasts/:id/shoppable-ad — admin dispatch",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminBearer}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v2/admin/broadcasts/{{broadcastId}}/shoppable-ad",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "admin",
                "broadcasts",
                "{{broadcastId}}",
                "shoppable-ad"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Programmatic ad dispatch from platform ops (source=`admin-api`). Same handler as 1.5 and the dashboard `trigger-shoppable-ad`, just under Bearer auth.\n\n**Called by**: Internal ops, cron jobs, integrations that don't have a clientApp apiKey.\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{success:true, activationId, product, sponsor}`",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n  \"sponsorId\": \"{{sponsorId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Dashboard operator (/api/*, session auth)",
      "description": "Dashboard UI endpoints. Session cookie required (dashboard login). **Not** part of the SDK contract — stays at `/api/*`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "5.1 POST /api/broadcasts/:id/trigger-shoppable-ad",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/broadcasts/{{broadcastId}}/trigger-shoppable-ad",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "broadcasts",
                "{{broadcastId}}",
                "trigger-shoppable-ad"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Purpose**: Operator-triggered shoppable ad from dashboard UI. Source=`dashboard`.\n\n**Called by**: `client/src/components/dashboard/BroadcastDetail.tsx` \"Fire shoppable ad\" button.\n\n**Expected**: 200 `{success:true, activationId, product, sponsor}`",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n  \"sponsorId\": \"{{sponsorId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "5.2 POST /api/broadcasts/:id/sponsor-slots/:slotId/execute",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
